1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,402
Therapy-speak doesn't only influence how we judge other people.

2
00:00:03,903 --> 00:00:07,325
It can also shape the explanations we accept for our own problems.

3
00:00:08,014 --> 00:00:14,960
Consider a worker who regularly puts in sixty hours a week, answers messages on
weekends, and struggles to get time off.

4
00:00:15,561 --> 00:00:16,742
She says she's burned out.

5
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:22,687
Her friends suggest setting boundaries, protecting her energy, and making more time for
herself.

6
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:24,829
Those suggestions may help.

7
00:00:25,237 --> 00:00:28,879
But suppose the employer expects everyone to maintain the same schedule.

8
00:00:29,299 --> 00:00:34,602
What happens when a problem partly created by an organization is addressed mainly
through personal behavior?

9
00:00:35,222 --> 00:00:37,984
Burnout is a particularly revealing example.

10
00:00:38,364 --> 00:00:46,528
The World Health Organization classifies it as an occupational phenomenon connected to
chronic workplace stress that hasn't been successfully managed.

11
00:00:46,808 --> 00:00:50,710
The WHO doesn't classify burnout itself as a medical condition.

12
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:54,532
And its definition explicitly connects the experience to work.

13
00:00:54,829 --> 00:00:58,872
Yet popular advice can place much of the responsibility on the employee.

14
00:00:59,072 --> 00:00:59,953
Learn to say no.

15
00:01:00,594 --> 00:01:01,314
Take more breaks.

16
00:01:01,634 --> 00:01:02,935
Develop a healthier routine.

17
00:01:03,256 --> 00:01:05,377
There may be good reasons to do those things.

18
00:01:05,798 --> 00:01:14,565
But none of them necessarily changes understaffing, unreasonable deadlines, or a
workplace culture that expects people to be constantly available.

19
00:01:15,045 --> 00:01:21,010
An individual can make better choices while still facing conditions that remain fundamentally
unreasonable.
